Installing chan_sccp
====================

Requirements: Asterisk 20 to 24 with its development headers, a C compiler,
GNU make, and the libxml2, libxslt, gettext and OpenSSL development packages.
Disable chan_skinny in modules.conf; it uses the same port.

  ./configure [--with-asterisk=/path/to/asterisk/prefix]
  make
  make check
  make install

make install copies chan_sccp.so to the Asterisk modules directory, the XML
documentation to Asterisk's documentation directory, and an example sccp.conf
to the configuration directory if none exists.

make install replaces the module file rather than writing into it, so the
running Asterisk keeps the old code until the module is unloaded and loaded
again (or Asterisk restarts). Never cp a new chan_sccp.so over the loaded one:
cp writes into the file the running process has mapped, and Asterisk crashes.
See doc/DEVELOPMENT.md.

./configure --help lists the build options. README.md lists the Asterisk
modules chan_sccp needs, and doc/UPGRADING.md covers upgrades from 4.x.
